                "evidence": "# UI Audit — Reminders (2026-11-02)\n\n## Stack\n- Framework: Vanilla JS + FastAPI serving one Jinja2 template (no JS framework, no jQuery/htmx)\n- Build tool: none\n- CSS: plain CSS in `app/static/styles.css` plus inline `style=` attributes in the template\n- State: none (the server list is re-fetched and re-rendered as HTML strings)\n- Design tokens: `app/static/styles.css` (`:root` block, 4 tokens, none used anywhere)\n- Run: `uvicorn app.main:app --reload` (run from the project root; inferred from `app/main.py`, no README/Procfile) → http://127.0.0.1:8000\n- Checks: none found\n\n## Pages / Routes (top 10)\n- `/` — `app/templates/index.html` (rendered by `app/main.py`)\n  - Tab \"Today\" (`#today`) — reminders not yet done\n  - Tab \"All reminders\" (`#all`) — every reminder\n  - Tab \"Settings\" (`#settings`) — notification time and Save\n- `/api/reminders` — `app/main.py` (JSON, not user-facing)\n- `/api/reminders/{id}/done` — `app/main.py` (JSON, not user-facing)\n\n## Style approach\nAlmost all styling is inline in `index.html` (11 `style=` attributes) with a small `styles.css` (13 lines) beside it. `styles.css` declares colour and spacing tokens, but nothing uses `var(--…)`. About 17 distinct colour values are hard-coded, several near-duplicates (`#fff`/`#ffffff`, three greys `#333/#444/#555` for the same tab buttons, `#2b6cb0` vs `#3182ce` blues).\n\n## Pain points\n\n### 🔴 High\n- Not responsive: `body` is fixed `width: 800px`, `.view` is `760px` and the input is `300px`. There is no `<meta name=\"viewport\">` and no media queries, so it breaks on phones.\n- Tokens exist but are unused: `--color-primary`, `--color-success` and others are defined, yet the same values are hard-coded in inline styles and CSS. This is the highest-leverage fix for a redesign.\n- Broken, inaccessible logo: `<img src=\"/static/logo.png\">` has no `alt`, and `logo.png` does not exist in `app/static/`.\n- Tabs and controls are not accessible: tab buttons have no `role=\"tablist\"`/`role=\"tab\"`/`aria-selected`, there are no `<header>`/`<nav>`/`<main>` landmarks, no `<html lang>`, the input has no `<label>`, and the grey-on-grey text (`#777` on `#fafafa`, `#a0aec0` done items) is likely under contrast guidelines.\n- Reminder titles are injected via `innerHTML` without escaping (`app/static/app.js`). A title containing HTML would render as markup (an XSS risk once users can add reminders).\n\n### 🟡 Medium\n- No loading, error or empty states: `loadReminders()` and `markDone()` have no spinner and no failure handling. `.empty` is styled but never used, so an empty Today tab is just blank.\n- Settings \"Save\" only shows `alert()`; nothing is sent to the backend and the time is not persisted. The design must either drop it or the backend must gain an endpoint.\n- No active-tab indicator: clicking a tab shows its view, but the buttons never show which one is selected.\n- \"Today\" means \"not done\", not \"due today\" (`app/static/app.js`), which is confusing next to the due dates shown.\n- The \"Done\" button is shown on already-done reminders, and the due date is raw ISO text (`2026-11-01`), with no overdue cue.\n\n### 🟢 Low\n- Inconsistent button styling: the tab, Done and Save buttons use three different looks.\n- Hard-coded English text throughout, with no i18n markers (fine unless a second language is planned).\n- No tests, lint or CI, so there are no automated checks to protect a port.\n\n## Recommendation\nConfirm scenario C: the app is tiny (about 100 lines, one page with three tabs) and keeping FastAPI + Jinja + vanilla JS is straightforward. Wire the tokens, fix the layout and accessibility, and decide the Settings behaviour in the design brief.\n"
              },
