                "evidence": "# UI Audit — Reminders (2026-11-02)\n\n## Stack\n- Framework: Vanilla JS + FastAPI serving one Jinja template (`app/templates/index.html`)\n- Build tool: none\n- CSS: plain CSS in `app/static/styles.css` (13 lines), plus inline `style=` in the template\n- State: none (DOM re-rendered from `/api/reminders`; in-memory list on the server)\n- Design tokens: `app/static/styles.css` (`:root` with 4 variables, none used anywhere)\n- Run: `uvicorn app.main:app --reload` (from project root; inferred from `app/main.py`, no README/Procfile) → http://127.0.0.1:8000 (uvicorn default port)\n- Checks: none found\n\n## Pages / Routes (top 10)\nSPA mode: one page, three client-side tabs.\n- `/` — `app/templates/index.html` (route in `app/main.py`)\n- Tab \"Today\" — `#today`, filled by `app/static/app.js` (not-done reminders)\n- Tab \"All reminders\" — `#all`, filled by `app/static/app.js`\n- Tab \"Settings\" — `#settings` (notification time input + Save)\n- `/api/reminders` (GET) and `/api/reminders/{id}/done` (POST) — `app/main.py` (data only, no UI)\n\n## Style approach\nStyling is split between a tiny stylesheet and about 10 inline `style=` attributes in the template, and `app.js` toggles visibility with inline `display`. The `:root` tokens (primary, success, text, space) are defined but never referenced with `var()`. About 17 unique hex colours are hard-coded, several of them near-duplicates (blues `#2b6cb0`/`#3182ce`, greys `#333`/`#444`/`#555`/`#777`).\n\n## Pain points\n\n### 🔴 High\n- Not responsive: `body` is fixed at `width: 800px` and `.view` at `760px`, and there is no `<meta name=\"viewport\">`, so it breaks on phones. No media queries at all.\n- Tokens exist but are unused: 4 `:root` variables, 0 `var()` uses, ~17 hard-coded colours and ~10 inline styles. Highest-leverage fix for a redesign.\n- Accessibility basics missing: no `alt` on the logo `<img>`, no `lang` on `<html>`, no `<header>`/`<nav>`/`<main>`, zero `aria-` attributes, tabs are plain buttons without `role=\"tab\"`/`aria-selected`, and the settings input has no `<label>`.\n- Broken logo: `/static/logo.png` is referenced but the file does not exist in `app/static/`.\n- Reminder titles are inserted with `innerHTML` unescaped (`app/static/app.js`), so a title containing HTML would render as markup. Needs fixing in the port (flag for the Developer).\n\n### 🟡 Medium\n- No loading or error state: the reminders `fetch` and the `markDone` POST show nothing while waiting or on failure. The tab area is blank until data arrives.\n- The Settings \"Save\" only shows `alert(...)`; nothing is stored and there is no backend route. The design must treat it as non-functional, or the Developer must add an endpoint.\n- \"Today\" tab shows every not-done reminder, not those due today. The `.empty` style exists but is never used, so there is no empty state.\n- \"Done\" button is shown on already-done reminders, and the active tab has no visual highlight.\n\n### 🟢 Low\n- All text is hard-coded English (no i18n markers found).\n- Page title is just \"Reminders\", with no favicon.\n- Tab and button padding and font sizes are inconsistent (22px greeting, default sizes elsewhere).\n\n## Recommendation\nConfirm scenario C: the app is tiny (about 100 lines in total, no file over 500) and the stack is simple, so a visual port into the existing template and stylesheet is quick. Required behaviour to preserve: 3 tabs, list with Done action, greeting with owner name, notification-time field.\n"
