                "evidence": "# UI Audit — Reminders (2026-11-02)\n\n## Stack\n- Framework: Vanilla JS + FastAPI serving one Jinja2 template (`app/templates/index.html`)\n- Build tool: none\n- CSS: plain CSS in `app/static/styles.css` (13 lines) plus inline `style=` in the template\n- State: none (DOM re-rendered from `/api/reminders`; in-memory list on the server)\n- Design tokens: `app/static/styles.css` (`:root` with 4 variables)\n- Run: `uvicorn app.main:app --reload` from the project root (paths like `app/static` are relative to it) → http://127.0.0.1:8000 (uvicorn default port; not stated in the files)\n- Checks: none found\n\n## Pages / Routes (top 10)\nSingle-page app: one server route, three client-side tabs.\n- `/` — `app/templates/index.html` (the page)\n  - Tab \"Today\" — `#today` (reminders not done)\n  - Tab \"All reminders\" — `#all`\n  - Tab \"Settings\" — `#settings` (notification time; Save only shows an `alert`)\n- `/api/reminders` (GET) — `app/main.py`, data only\n- `/api/reminders/{id}/done` (POST) — `app/main.py`, data only\n\n## Style approach\nStyling is split between a tiny stylesheet and inline `style=` attributes on 11 elements in the template. The stylesheet declares colour/spacing variables but never uses them (`var(` appears 0 times), so every colour is a hard-coded value. The page is fixed at 800px wide.\n\n## Pain points\n\n### 🔴 High\n- Not responsive: `<body>` is `width: 800px` and `.view` is `width: 760px`; no `<meta name=\"viewport\">` and no media queries, so the page will not fit a phone.\n- Tokens exist but are unused: 4 variables in `:root`, 0 `var()` uses, about 17 distinct hard-coded colours (e.g. three near-identical greys `#333/#444/#555` on the tab buttons, two blues `#2b6cb0` and `#3182ce`). Highest-leverage fix for a redesign.\n- Accessibility basics missing: no `lang` on `<html>`, logo `<img>` has no `alt` (and `/static/logo.png` does not exist in the repo, so it renders broken), no `<header>/<nav>/<main>`, tabs are plain buttons with no `role=\"tablist\"/\"tab\"`, `aria-selected` or `aria-controls`; 0 `aria-` attributes for 4 buttons. The active tab is also not visually indicated.\n- Reminder titles are inserted with `innerHTML` unescaped (`app.js:17-22`), so a title containing HTML would be rendered as markup. Fix while porting the list rendering.\n\n### 🟡 Medium\n- No loading or error state: both `fetch` calls (`app.js:10`, `app.js:27`) show nothing while waiting and nothing on failure; the Done button is not disabled during the request. The `.empty` style is defined but never used, so an empty list is a blank area.\n- Settings does nothing real: Save only runs `alert(...)`; nothing is stored and there is no backend endpoint for it. The design must either drop it or the Developer must add an endpoint.\n- The \"Today\" tab is just \"not done\", not filtered by date, which can mislead users once the design labels it by day.\n\n### 🟢 Low\n- Hard-coded English text throughout (no i18n markers); fine if the app stays English-only.\n- Inline `onclick=\"markDone(...)\"` handlers and `display:none` toggling in JS rather than a CSS class.\n- No page `<meta description>` or favicon.\n\n## Recommendation\nConfirm scenario C: the project is tiny (4 files, all under 500 lines), the stack is simple, and a new look can be ported into the existing template and stylesheet. Note for the design brief: the Settings screen has no backend behind it.\n"
